<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nguyễn lords</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1558">1558</a>–<a href="/years/1777">1777</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Nguyen lords, Đàng Trong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nguyễn lords were a family of hereditary rulers who governed southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> in the name of the Lê emperors from 1558. From their capital at Phú Xuân they resisted the Trịnh lords of the north in wars from 1627 to 1672, and extended Vietnamese settlement into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-river">Mekong</a> delta. Overthrown by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tay-son-dynasty">Tây Sơn</a>, their heir founded the Nguyễn dynasty in 1802.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nguyen-lords.jpg" alt="Nguyễn lords" width="320" height="533" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Own work by uploader · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vietnam1650.GIF" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>From 1627 to 1672 the Trịnh fought seven major campaigns against the <b>Nguyễn lords</b> in the south, using war elephants, large infantry forces and fleets of galleys; the Nguyễn held them off behind fortified walls near Đồng Hới and with cannon cast with Portuguese help, and in 1643…</blockquote><a href="/empire/later-le-dynasty">Later Le dynasty · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The Nguyen dynasty descended from the <b>Nguyen lords</b>, who had ruled southern Vietnam (Dang Trong) since the sixteenth century, from 1687 with their seat at Phu Xuan, the later Hue.</blockquote><a href="/empire/nguyen-dynasty">Nguyen dynasty · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Nguyen lords</b> defended the Dong Hoi walls against Trinh attacks between 1627 and 1672 with the help of Portuguese cannon.</blockquote><a href="/state/nguyen-lords">Nguyen lords</a></li></ul></section>
